full_article:
Bangladesh and Nepal have agreed to strengthen bilateral cooperation in the health sector, with discussions focusing on pharmaceutical trade and medical education.

The agreement came during a bilateral meeting between Bangladesh's Health and Family Welfare Minister Sardar Md Sakhawat Husain and Nepal's Health and Food Security Minister Nisha Mehta in Sri Lanka's Colombo today (11 November).

The meeting was held on the sidelines of the first Bimstec Health Ministers' Meeting.

