During the meeting, the two ministers discussed ways to expand cooperation in the health sector, particularly increasing trade in pharmaceutical products between Bangladesh and Nepal and creating more opportunities for Nepali students to enrol in Bangladeshi medical colleges.

They also emphasised strengthening bilateral relations and communication in the health sector and identifying new areas of cooperation that would benefit both countries.

googletag.cmd.push(function() { googletag.display("dfp-ad-tbs_rectangle_snd_mobile"); });

The discussions also covered opportunities to enhance collaboration through international and regional platforms, including Bimstec.

Both ministers reaffirmed their commitment to working together to address shared health challenges and promote regional healthcare development.

googletag.cmd.push(function() { googletag.display("dfp-ad-tbs_rectangle_snd_mobile02"); });

The meeting reflected the two countries' interest in further strengthening their friendly relations and expanding mutually beneficial cooperation in the health sector.

